<html lang="en-GB">
<head><meta charSet="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght,SOFT,WONK@0,9..144,300..800,0..100,0..1;1,9..144,300..800,0..100,0..1&amp;family=Karla:ital,wght@0,300..800;1,400..600&amp;display=swap" data-precedence="default"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/index-Ud4hi37y.css" type="text/css" data-precedence="default"/><title>Slat &amp; Weave — garden furniture care notes</title><meta name="theme-color" content="#f4eddd"/><meta property="og:title" content="Slat &amp; Weave — garden furniture care notes"/><meta property="og:description" content="Practical care, repair and buying notes for teak, rattan, metal and cushions — written from a furniture restoration bench in Devon."/><meta property="og:type" content="website"/><meta name="description" content="Practical garden furniture tips: teak silvering, rattan sagging, rust on powder coat, mildew in cushions, winter storage and what to check when buying second-hand."/><link rel="modulepreload" href="assets/index-DSZlduRa.js"/><link rel="modulepreload" href="assets/index-CO2KyX7o.js"/><link rel="modulepreload" href="assets/illustration-D-fSZOkv.js"/><link rel="modulepreload" href="assets/tip-card-iFdTrX5_.js"/><link rel="icon" href="favicon.ico"/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/"/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com/" crossorigin="anonymous"/></head><body class="flex min-h-screen flex-col bg-paper text-ink"><div class="grain-layer" aria-hidden="true"></div><header class="sticky top-0 z-40 border-b border-ink/12 bg-paper/88 backdrop-blur-md"><div class="mx-auto flex max-w-6xl flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 px-5 py-3 sm:px-8"><a aria-label="Slat &amp; Weave, home" class="group flex items-center gap-2.5 active" href="index.html" data-status="active" aria-current="page"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" class="h-8 w-8 shrink-0 text-teak"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M4 10h24M4 16h24M4 22h24" opacity="0.9"></path><path d="M8 4c0 8 16 8 16 16s-16 4-16 4" stroke-width="2.2" class="text-moss" stroke="currentColor" opacity="0.45"></path></g></svg><span class="flex flex-col leading-none"><span class="display text-[1.32rem] text-moss transition-colors group-hover:text-teak">Slat &amp; Weave</span><span class="eyebrow mt-1 text-[0.58rem] text-ink-faint">Outdoor furniture care</span></span></a><nav class="ml-auto flex items-center gap-5 text-[0.93rem] sm:gap-7"><a href="tips.html" class="link-draw font-medium text-ink-soft transition-colors hover:text-teak aria-[current=page]:text-moss">All tips</a><a href="calendar.html" class="link-draw font-medium text-ink-soft transition-colors hover:text-teak aria-[current=page]:text-moss">Care calendar</a><a href="about.html" class="link-draw font-medium text-ink-soft transition-colors hover:text-teak aria-[current=page]:text-moss">About</a></nav></div><div class="rule-teak h-[2px] w-full"></div></header><main class="flex-1"><!--$--><section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-ink/12"><div class="hatch pointer-events-none absolute top-0 right-0 hidden h-full w-[38%] lg:block" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="relative mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-10 px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-24 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_0.85fr] lg:gap-6 lg:py-28"><div><p class="eyebrow rise text-teak">Care notes · not product reviews</p><h1 class="display rise mt-5 text-[clamp(2.65rem,7.2vw,5.1rem)] text-ink [animation-delay:90ms]">Nothing out here<span class="block text-moss">wears out.</span><span class="block italic text-ink-soft">It gets forgotten</span><span class="block">in October.</span></h1><p class="rise mt-7 max-w-xl text-[1.06rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft [animation-delay:180ms]">Teak that has gone grey is fine. Rattan that has gone soft usually is not a weave problem. This is a working file of<!-- --> <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">12<!-- --> specific jobs</strong> <!-- -->— what to look at, in what order, and which of it you can safely ignore.</p><div class="rise mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-7 gap-y-4 [animation-delay:260ms]"><a href="tips.html" class="eyebrow rounded-sm bg-moss px-6 py-3.5 text-paper shadow-lift transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:bg-teak hover:shadow-lift-hi">Start with the index</a><a href="calendar.html" class="link-draw text-[0.96rem] font-medium text-moss">Or jump to what is due this season</a></div></div><div class="relative hidden lg:block"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Teak &amp; hardwood illustration" class="swing-in h-auto w-full text-moss/70 [animation-delay:200ms]"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M26 96V26M94 96V26"></path><path d="M26 34h68M26 46h68M26 58h68" stroke-width="1.2"></path><path d="M16 70h88M16 70v7h88v-7"></path><path d="M30 70v7M46 70v7M62 70v7M78 70v7" stroke-width="1"></path><path d="M16 70V58M104 70V58M16 58l10-4M104 58l-10-4"></path><path d="M24 77v27M96 77v27M24 92h12M84 92h12"></path><path d="M8 104h104" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="1 5"></path></g></svg><p class="absolute -bottom-2 right-2 max-w-[15rem] border-l-2 border-teak pl-3 text-[0.8rem] leading-snug text-ink-faint italic">A silvered teak bench is structurally identical to a honey one. The grey layer is a tenth of a millimetre deep.</p></div></div></section><section class="border-b border-ink/12 bg-paper-warm"><div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-18 sm:px-8 sm:py-24"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-4"><h2 class="display text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.8rem)] text-moss">Three things that explain<br/>most of it</h2><p class="eyebrow max-w-xs text-ink-faint">Learn these and you can work out the rest yourself</p></div><ol class="mt-14 space-y-12"><li class="grid gap-x-8 gap-y-3 border-t border-ink/15 pt-7 sm:grid-cols-[5rem_1fr] "><span class="display text-[2.6rem] leading-none text-teak/70">01</span><div><h3 class="display-soft text-[1.42rem] leading-tight text-ink">Water, not cold, does the damage</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-[58ch] text-[0.97rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Ice expands about 9% every time it freezes in a joint, a tube or a pore. Almost every winter repair traces back to water that had nowhere to drain. Lift legs off wet stone, keep drain holes clear, and store things tilted.</p></div></li><li class="grid gap-x-8 gap-y-3 border-t border-ink/15 pt-7 sm:grid-cols-[5rem_1fr] lg:ml-14"><span class="display text-[2.6rem] leading-none text-teak/70">02</span><div><h3 class="display-soft text-[1.42rem] leading-tight text-ink">Find the cause under the symptom</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-[58ch] text-[0.97rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A sagging rattan seat is usually two perished webbing straps. A rusty leg is usually a missing plastic foot. Cushion mildew is usually a foam core that never dried. Treat the visible thing and you will be doing it again next year.</p></div></li><li class="grid gap-x-8 gap-y-3 border-t border-ink/15 pt-7 sm:grid-cols-[5rem_1fr] lg:ml-28"><span class="display text-[2.6rem] leading-none text-teak/70">03</span><div><h3 class="display-soft text-[1.42rem] leading-tight text-ink">Inspect first, shop once</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-[58ch] text-[0.97rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Walk the whole set with a notebook before you buy anything. One order of plastic feet, touch-up enamel and oxygen bleach turns three separate weekends into a single hour.</p></div></li></ol></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-18 sm:px-8 sm:py-24"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-4"><div><p class="eyebrow text-teak">Read first</p><h2 class="display mt-3 text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.8rem)] text-ink">The notes people need soonest</h2></div><a href="tips.html" class="link-draw text-[0.95rem] font-medium text-moss">All <!-- -->12<!-- --> notes →</a></div><div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3"><div class="lg:col-span-2 lg:row-span-2"><a href="tips/teak-silver-or-honey.html" style="animation-delay:0ms" class="group rise relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-sm border border-ink/15 bg-paper-warm p-6 shadow-lift transition-all duration-500 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-moss/40 hover:shadow-lift-hi sm:p-7"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Teak &amp; hardwood illustration" class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-6 text-moss/22 transition-all duration-700 group-hover:text-teak/35 group-hover:scale-105 -bottom-8 h-52 w-52"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M26 96V26M94 96V26"></path><path d="M26 34h68M26 46h68M26 58h68" stroke-width="1.2"></path><path d="M16 70h88M16 70v7h88v-7"></path><path d="M30 70v7M46 70v7M62 70v7M78 70v7" stroke-width="1"></path><path d="M16 70V58M104 70V58M16 58l10-4M104 58l-10-4"></path><path d="M24 77v27M96 77v27M24 92h12M84 92h12"></path><path d="M8 104h104" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="1 5"></path></g></svg><p class="eyebrow flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2.5 gap-y-1 text-ink-faint"><span class="text-teak">Teak &amp; hardwood</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-ink/25">/</span><span>Ten minutes</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-ink/25">/</span><span>2<!-- --> min read</span></p><h3 class="display mt-3.5 max-w-[22ch] text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-moss text-[clamp(1.6rem,2.6vw,2.15rem)]">Teak: let it silver, or keep it honey?</h3><p class="relative mt-3 text-[0.94rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft max-w-[46ch]">Silvering is a surface change, not decay. Here is what each choice actually costs you in time and money over ten years.</p><span class="eyebrow relative mt-auto pt-7 text-moss">Read the note<span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-1.5 inline-block transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1">→</span></span></a></div><a href="tips/rattan-sagging-weave.html" style="animation-delay:70ms" class="group rise relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-sm border border-ink/15 bg-paper-warm p-6 shadow-lift transition-all duration-500 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-moss/40 hover:shadow-lift-hi sm:p-7"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Rattan &amp; wicker illustration" class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-6 text-moss/22 transition-all duration-700 group-hover:text-teak/35 group-hover:scale-105 -bottom-6 h-40 w-40"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M28 40c0-13 12-20 32-20s32 7 32 20v22c0 12-14 18-32 18s-32-6-32-18z"></path><path d="M28 44c8 6 20 9 32 9s24-3 32-9" stroke-width="1.2"></path><g stroke-width="0.9" opacity="0.85"><path d="M32 52l18 22M44 50l18 24M56 50l18 24M68 50l18 22M80 52l10 14"></path><path d="M88 52L70 74M76 50L58 74M64 50L46 74M52 50L34 72M40 52l-8 12"></path></g><path d="M34 62c8 5 18 7 26 7s18-2 26-7"></path><path d="M36 78l-6 26M84 78l6 26M42 96h36"></path><path d="M10 104h100" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="1 5"></path></g></svg><p class="eyebrow flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2.5 gap-y-1 text-ink-faint"><span class="text-teak">Rattan &amp; wicker</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-ink/25">/</span><span>An afternoon</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-ink/25">/</span><span>2<!-- --> min read</span></p><h3 class="display mt-3.5 max-w-[22ch] text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-moss text-[1.42rem]">Re-tension a sagging rattan seat without re-weaving it</h3><p class="relative mt-3 text-[0.94rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft max-w-[38ch]">A dish-shaped synthetic rattan seat is usually a stretched frame problem, not a weave problem. Ten minutes with webbing fixes most of them.</p><span class="eyebrow relative mt-auto pt-7 text-moss">Read the note<span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-1.5 inline-block transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1">→</span></span></a><a href="tips/rust-on-powder-coat.html" style="animation-delay:140ms" class="group rise relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-sm border border-ink/15 bg-paper-warm p-6 shadow-lift transition-all duration-500 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-moss/40 hover:shadow-lift-hi sm:p-7"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Metal &amp; powder coat illustration" class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-6 text-moss/22 transition-all duration-700 group-hover:text-teak/35 group-hover:scale-105 -bottom-6 h-40 w-40"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M34 74V40c0-14 8-22 26-22s26 8 26 22v34"></path><path d="M40 40h40" stroke-width="1.1"></path><g stroke-width="0" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5"><circle cx="46" cy="52" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="56" cy="52" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="66" cy="52" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="76" cy="52" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="51" cy="62" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="61" cy="62" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="71" cy="62" r="1.5"></circle></g><ellipse cx="60" cy="76" rx="34" ry="9"></ellipse><path d="M26 76c0 5 15 9 34 9s34-4 34-9" stroke-width="1.1"></path><path d="M32 80l-8 24M88 80l8 24M42 84l-4 20M78 84l4 20"></path><path d="M8 104h104" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="1 5"></path></g></svg><p class="eyebrow flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2.5 gap-y-1 text-ink-faint"><span class="text-teak">Metal &amp; powder coat</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-ink/25">/</span><span>Ten minutes</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-ink/25">/</span><span>2<!-- --> min read</span></p><h3 class="display mt-3.5 max-w-[22ch] text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-moss text-[1.42rem]">Catch rust on powder-coated steel in the two weeks that matter</h3><p class="relative mt-3 text-[0.94rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft max-w-[38ch]">A powder coat fails at a single chip and then lifts outward. There is a short window where a cotton bud of touch-up paint saves the frame.</p><span class="eyebrow relative mt-auto pt-7 text-moss">Read the note<span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-1.5 inline-block transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1">→</span></span></a><a href="tips/mildew-in-cushions.html" style="animation-delay:210ms" class="group rise relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-sm border border-ink/15 bg-paper-warm p-6 shadow-lift transition-all duration-500 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-moss/40 hover:shadow-lift-hi sm:p-7"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Cushions &amp; fabric illustration" class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-6 text-moss/22 transition-all duration-700 group-hover:text-teak/35 group-hover:scale-105 -bottom-6 h-40 w-40"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 66c0-6 4-9 10-9h60c6 0 10 3 10 9v14c0 6-4 9-10 9H30c-6 0-10-3-10-9z"></path><path d="M20 72h80" stroke-width="0.9" stroke-dasharray="3 3"></path><path d="M28 36c0-6 4-10 10-10h58c6 0 10 4 10 10v12c0 6-4 9-10 9H38c-6 0-10-3-10-9z"></path><path d="M28 42h78" stroke-width="0.9" stroke-dasharray="3 3"></path><circle cx="68" cy="42" r="3" stroke-width="1.3"></circle><g stroke-width="1.2" opacity="0.7"><path d="M44 22c0-3 3-6 3-6s3 3 3 6a3 3 0 11-6 0z"></path><path d="M86 18c0-2.5 2.5-5 2.5-5s2.5 2.5 2.5 5a2.5 2.5 0 11-5 0z"></path></g></g></svg><p class="eyebrow flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2.5 gap-y-1 text-ink-faint"><span class="text-teak">Cushions &amp; fabric</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-ink/25">/</span><span>An afternoon</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-ink/25">/</span><span>2<!-- --> min read</span></p><h3 class="display mt-3.5 max-w-[22ch] text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-moss text-[1.42rem]">Get mildew out of outdoor cushions (and the foam underneath)</h3><p class="relative mt-3 text-[0.94rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft max-w-[38ch]">Black speckling on the cover is the symptom. If the foam core is still damp you will be doing this again in a fortnight.</p><span class="eyebrow relative mt-auto pt-7 text-moss">Read the note<span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-1.5 inline-block transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1">→</span></span></a><a href="tips/overwintering-no-shed.html" style="animation-delay:280ms" class="group rise relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-sm border border-ink/15 bg-paper-warm p-6 shadow-lift transition-all duration-500 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-moss/40 hover:shadow-lift-hi sm:p-7"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Storage &amp; seasons illustration" class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-6 text-moss/22 transition-all duration-700 group-hover:text-teak/35 group-hover:scale-105 -bottom-6 h-40 w-40"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M60 16c22 0 30 10 34 28l6 34c-12 5-26 7-40 7s-28-2-40-7l6-34c4-18 12-28 34-28z"></path><path d="M48 20l-6 58M72 20l6 58M60 18v62" stroke-width="0.9" opacity="0.7"></path><path d="M20 78c7 4 13 5 20 4s13-4 20-4 13 3 20 4 13 0 20-4" stroke-width="1.2"></path><path d="M34 82v16M52 82v16M68 82v16M86 82v16"></path><path d="M29 98h10M47 98h10M63 98h10M81 98h10" stroke-width="2.4"></path><path d="M8 104h104" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="1 5"></path></g></svg><p class="eyebrow flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2.5 gap-y-1 text-ink-faint"><span class="text-teak">Storage &amp; seasons</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-ink/25">/</span><span>An afternoon</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="text-ink/25">/</span><span>2<!-- --> min read</span></p><h3 class="display mt-3.5 max-w-[22ch] text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-moss text-[1.42rem]">Overwinter a full set when you have no shed</h3><p class="relative mt-3 text-[0.94rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft max-w-[38ch]">Most winter damage is freeze-thaw in trapped water, not cold. You can protect a set in a flat with three bin bags and some careful stacking.</p><span class="eyebrow relative mt-auto pt-7 text-moss">Read the note<span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-1.5 inline-block transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1">→</span></span></a></div></section><section class="border-y border-ink/12 bg-paper-warm"><div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-18 sm:px-8 sm:py-24"><p class="eyebrow text-teak">Straight to your problem</p><h2 class="display mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.8rem)] text-ink">Different materials fail in completely different ways</h2><div class="mt-12 divide-y divide-ink/12 border-t border-ink/12"><a href="topics/teak-and-hardwood.html" class="group grid grid-cols-[3.5rem_1fr] items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 py-6 transition-colors hover:bg-paper/70 sm:grid-cols-[4.5rem_minmax(0,14rem)_1fr_auto] sm:gap-x-8"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Teak &amp; hardwood illustration" class="h-14 w-14 text-moss/50 transition-all duration-500 group-hover:text-teak group-hover:-rotate-3"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M26 96V26M94 96V26"></path><path d="M26 34h68M26 46h68M26 58h68" stroke-width="1.2"></path><path d="M16 70h88M16 70v7h88v-7"></path><path d="M30 70v7M46 70v7M62 70v7M78 70v7" stroke-width="1"></path><path d="M16 70V58M104 70V58M16 58l10-4M104 58l-10-4"></path><path d="M24 77v27M96 77v27M24 92h12M84 92h12"></path><path d="M8 104h104" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="1 5"></path></g></svg><h3 class="display-soft text-[1.28rem] leading-tight text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-teak">Teak &amp; hardwood</h3><p class="col-span-2 max-w-[62ch] text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft sm:col-span-1">Silvering, sealing, splits and slack bolts. Most hardwood problems are cosmetic; the ones that are not show up in the end grain.</p><span class="eyebrow hidden shrink-0 text-ink-faint tabular-nums sm:block">2<!-- --> <!-- -->notes<span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-2 inline-block text-teak opacity-0 transition-all duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1 group-hover:opacity-100">→</span></span><span class="eyebrow text-ink-faint sm:hidden">2<!-- --> <!-- -->notes<!-- --> →</span></a><a href="topics/rattan-and-wicker.html" class="group grid grid-cols-[3.5rem_1fr] items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 py-6 transition-colors hover:bg-paper/70 sm:grid-cols-[4.5rem_minmax(0,14rem)_1fr_auto] sm:gap-x-8"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Rattan &amp; wicker illustration" class="h-14 w-14 text-moss/50 transition-all duration-500 group-hover:text-teak group-hover:-rotate-3"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M28 40c0-13 12-20 32-20s32 7 32 20v22c0 12-14 18-32 18s-32-6-32-18z"></path><path d="M28 44c8 6 20 9 32 9s24-3 32-9" stroke-width="1.2"></path><g stroke-width="0.9" opacity="0.85"><path d="M32 52l18 22M44 50l18 24M56 50l18 24M68 50l18 22M80 52l10 14"></path><path d="M88 52L70 74M76 50L58 74M64 50L46 74M52 50L34 72M40 52l-8 12"></path></g><path d="M34 62c8 5 18 7 26 7s18-2 26-7"></path><path d="M36 78l-6 26M84 78l6 26M42 96h36"></path><path d="M10 104h100" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="1 5"></path></g></svg><h3 class="display-soft text-[1.28rem] leading-tight text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-teak">Rattan &amp; wicker</h3><p class="col-span-2 max-w-[62ch] text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft sm:col-span-1">Synthetic weave fails in predictable ways, and the frame underneath usually goes first. How to tell which one you have.</p><span class="eyebrow hidden shrink-0 text-ink-faint tabular-nums sm:block">1<!-- --> <!-- -->note<span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-2 inline-block text-teak opacity-0 transition-all duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1 group-hover:opacity-100">→</span></span><span class="eyebrow text-ink-faint sm:hidden">1<!-- --> <!-- -->note<!-- --> →</span></a><a href="topics/metal-and-powder-coat.html" class="group grid grid-cols-[3.5rem_1fr] items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 py-6 transition-colors hover:bg-paper/70 sm:grid-cols-[4.5rem_minmax(0,14rem)_1fr_auto] sm:gap-x-8"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Metal &amp; powder coat illustration" class="h-14 w-14 text-moss/50 transition-all duration-500 group-hover:text-teak group-hover:-rotate-3"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M34 74V40c0-14 8-22 26-22s26 8 26 22v34"></path><path d="M40 40h40" stroke-width="1.1"></path><g stroke-width="0" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5"><circle cx="46" cy="52" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="56" cy="52" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="66" cy="52" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="76" cy="52" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="51" cy="62" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="61" cy="62" r="1.5"></circle><circle cx="71" cy="62" r="1.5"></circle></g><ellipse cx="60" cy="76" rx="34" ry="9"></ellipse><path d="M26 76c0 5 15 9 34 9s34-4 34-9" stroke-width="1.1"></path><path d="M32 80l-8 24M88 80l8 24M42 84l-4 20M78 84l4 20"></path><path d="M8 104h104" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="1 5"></path></g></svg><h3 class="display-soft text-[1.28rem] leading-tight text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-teak">Metal &amp; powder coat</h3><p class="col-span-2 max-w-[62ch] text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft sm:col-span-1">Coating protects until it is breached, then it lifts outward. Catching that early is the whole discipline.</p><span class="eyebrow hidden shrink-0 text-ink-faint tabular-nums sm:block">2<!-- --> <!-- -->notes<span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-2 inline-block text-teak opacity-0 transition-all duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1 group-hover:opacity-100">→</span></span><span class="eyebrow text-ink-faint sm:hidden">2<!-- --> <!-- -->notes<!-- --> →</span></a><a href="topics/cushions-and-fabric.html" class="group grid grid-cols-[3.5rem_1fr] items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 py-6 transition-colors hover:bg-paper/70 sm:grid-cols-[4.5rem_minmax(0,14rem)_1fr_auto] sm:gap-x-8"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Cushions &amp; fabric illustration" class="h-14 w-14 text-moss/50 transition-all duration-500 group-hover:text-teak group-hover:-rotate-3"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 66c0-6 4-9 10-9h60c6 0 10 3 10 9v14c0 6-4 9-10 9H30c-6 0-10-3-10-9z"></path><path d="M20 72h80" stroke-width="0.9" stroke-dasharray="3 3"></path><path d="M28 36c0-6 4-10 10-10h58c6 0 10 4 10 10v12c0 6-4 9-10 9H38c-6 0-10-3-10-9z"></path><path d="M28 42h78" stroke-width="0.9" stroke-dasharray="3 3"></path><circle cx="68" cy="42" r="3" stroke-width="1.3"></circle><g stroke-width="1.2" opacity="0.7"><path d="M44 22c0-3 3-6 3-6s3 3 3 6a3 3 0 11-6 0z"></path><path d="M86 18c0-2.5 2.5-5 2.5-5s2.5 2.5 2.5 5a2.5 2.5 0 11-5 0z"></path></g></g></svg><h3 class="display-soft text-[1.28rem] leading-tight text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-teak">Cushions &amp; fabric</h3><p class="col-span-2 max-w-[62ch] text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft sm:col-span-1">Covers clean up easily. The foam inside is what decides whether the mildew comes back in a fortnight.</p><span class="eyebrow hidden shrink-0 text-ink-faint tabular-nums sm:block">1<!-- --> <!-- -->note<span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-2 inline-block text-teak opacity-0 transition-all duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1 group-hover:opacity-100">→</span></span><span class="eyebrow text-ink-faint sm:hidden">1<!-- --> <!-- -->note<!-- --> →</span></a><a href="topics/storage-and-seasons.html" class="group grid grid-cols-[3.5rem_1fr] items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 py-6 transition-colors hover:bg-paper/70 sm:grid-cols-[4.5rem_minmax(0,14rem)_1fr_auto] sm:gap-x-8"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Storage &amp; seasons illustration" class="h-14 w-14 text-moss/50 transition-all duration-500 group-hover:text-teak group-hover:-rotate-3"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M60 16c22 0 30 10 34 28l6 34c-12 5-26 7-40 7s-28-2-40-7l6-34c4-18 12-28 34-28z"></path><path d="M48 20l-6 58M72 20l6 58M60 18v62" stroke-width="0.9" opacity="0.7"></path><path d="M20 78c7 4 13 5 20 4s13-4 20-4 13 3 20 4 13 0 20-4" stroke-width="1.2"></path><path d="M34 82v16M52 82v16M68 82v16M86 82v16"></path><path d="M29 98h10M47 98h10M63 98h10M81 98h10" stroke-width="2.4"></path><path d="M8 104h104" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="1 5"></path></g></svg><h3 class="display-soft text-[1.28rem] leading-tight text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-teak">Storage &amp; seasons</h3><p class="col-span-2 max-w-[62ch] text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft sm:col-span-1">Winter damage is freeze-thaw in trapped water, not cold. Everything here is about getting water out and keeping it out.</p><span class="eyebrow hidden shrink-0 text-ink-faint tabular-nums sm:block">2<!-- --> <!-- -->notes<span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-2 inline-block text-teak opacity-0 transition-all duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1 group-hover:opacity-100">→</span></span><span class="eyebrow text-ink-faint sm:hidden">2<!-- --> <!-- -->notes<!-- --> →</span></a><a href="topics/buying-advice.html" class="group grid grid-cols-[3.5rem_1fr] items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 py-6 transition-colors hover:bg-paper/70 sm:grid-cols-[4.5rem_minmax(0,14rem)_1fr_auto] sm:gap-x-8"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Buying advice illustration" class="h-14 w-14 text-moss/50 transition-all duration-500 group-hover:text-teak group-hover:-rotate-3"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M52 22h40c5 0 8 3 8 8v40c0 5-3 8-8 8H52L22 50z"></path><circle cx="44" cy="50" r="4"></circle><path d="M100 34c10-6 12-14 8-20" stroke-width="1.2"></path><path d="M62 40h28M62 50h28M62 60h18" stroke-width="1.1" opacity="0.75"></path><circle cx="46" cy="82" r="15" stroke-width="1.9"></circle><path d="M57 93l12 12" stroke-width="2.4"></path><path d="M40 82h12M46 76v12" stroke-width="1.1" opacity="0.8"></path></g></svg><h3 class="display-soft text-[1.28rem] leading-tight text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-teak">Buying advice</h3><p class="col-span-2 max-w-[62ch] text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft sm:col-span-1">What to check, what to ignore, and which flaws are worth a discount because they take an afternoon to reverse.</p><span class="eyebrow hidden shrink-0 text-ink-faint tabular-nums sm:block">3<!-- --> <!-- -->notes<span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-2 inline-block text-teak opacity-0 transition-all duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1 group-hover:opacity-100">→</span></span><span class="eyebrow text-ink-faint sm:hidden">3<!-- --> <!-- -->notes<!-- --> →</span></a><a href="topics/layout.html" class="group grid grid-cols-[3.5rem_1fr] items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 py-6 transition-colors hover:bg-paper/70 sm:grid-cols-[4.5rem_minmax(0,14rem)_1fr_auto] sm:gap-x-8"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Layout illustration" class="h-14 w-14 text-moss/50 transition-all duration-500 group-hover:text-teak group-hover:-rotate-3"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 24h92v72H14z"></path><path d="M14 96h92" stroke-width="3"></path><path d="M22 96v6M38 96v6M54 96v6M70 96v6M86 96v6M100 96v6" stroke-width="1.2"></path><path d="M14 24h92" stroke-width="3"></path><g stroke-width="0.9" opacity="0.6"><path d="M16 24l-6-8M32 24l-6-8M48 24l-6-8M64 24l-6-8M80 24l-6-8M96 24l-6-8"></path></g><path d="M26 38h24v22H26zM58 38h24v22H58z" stroke-width="1.4"></path><path d="M26 38h24M58 38h24" stroke-width="2.6"></path><circle cx="94" cy="52" r="9" stroke-width="1.4"></circle><path d="M20 70v20M17 73l3-3 3 3M17 87l3 3 3-3" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.8"></path></g></svg><h3 class="display-soft text-[1.28rem] leading-tight text-ink transition-colors group-hover:text-teak">Layout</h3><p class="col-span-2 max-w-[62ch] text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft sm:col-span-1">Small spaces are decided by depth, not area. The geometry of fitting seating into 1.4 metres.</p><span class="eyebrow hidden shrink-0 text-ink-faint tabular-nums sm:block">1<!-- --> <!-- -->note<span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-2 inline-block text-teak opacity-0 transition-all duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1 group-hover:opacity-100">→</span></span><span class="eyebrow text-ink-faint sm:hidden">1<!-- --> <!-- -->note<!-- --> →</span></a></div></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-18 sm:px-8 sm:py-24"><div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-sm border-2 border-moss bg-paper-warm"><svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="Storage &amp; seasons illustration" class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-10 -bottom-16 h-72 w-72 text-moss/12"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M60 16c22 0 30 10 34 28l6 34c-12 5-26 7-40 7s-28-2-40-7l6-34c4-18 12-28 34-28z"></path><path d="M48 20l-6 58M72 20l6 58M60 18v62" stroke-width="0.9" opacity="0.7"></path><path d="M20 78c7 4 13 5 20 4s13-4 20-4 13 3 20 4 13 0 20-4" stroke-width="1.2"></path><path d="M34 82v16M52 82v16M68 82v16M86 82v16"></path><path d="M29 98h10M47 98h10M63 98h10M81 98h10" stroke-width="2.4"></path><path d="M8 104h104" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="1 5"></path></g></svg><div class="relative max-w-2xl p-8 sm:p-12"><p class="eyebrow text-teak">The calendar</p><h2 class="display mt-3 text-[clamp(1.8rem,3.6vw,2.5rem)] text-moss">Most of this is timing, not skill</h2><p class="mt-5 text-[1rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A rust blister has about two weeks of wet weather before the repair stops being a cotton bud and starts being a grinder. Foam needs two to four days to dry, so it has to be the first thing you start, not the last. The calendar puts every note in the week it actually belongs.</p><ul class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2"><li class="eyebrow text-ink-faint"><span class="text-moss">Spring</span> <span class="tabular-nums">4</span></li><li class="eyebrow text-ink-faint"><span class="text-moss">Summer</span> <span class="tabular-nums">2</span></li><li class="eyebrow text-ink-faint"><span class="text-moss">Autumn</span> <span class="tabular-nums">2</span></li><li class="eyebrow text-ink-faint"><span class="text-moss">Any time</span> <span class="tabular-nums">4</span></li></ul><a href="calendar.html" class="eyebrow mt-9 inline-block border-b-2 border-teak pb-1 text-moss transition-colors hover:text-teak">Open the care calendar →</a></div></div></section><script>(function(t){let s;try{s=JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem(t.storageKey)||"{}")}catch(e){console.error(e);return}const c=t.key||window.history.state?.__TSR_key,r=c?s[c]:void 0;if(t.shouldScrollRestoration&&r&&typeof r=="object"&&Object.keys(r).length>0){for(const e in r){const o=r[e];if(!o||typeof o!="object")continue;const l=o.scrollX,i=o.scrollY;if(!(!Number.isFinite(l)||!Number.isFinite(i))){if(e==="window")window.scrollTo({top:i,left:l,behavior:t.behavior});else if(e){let n;try{n=document.querySelector(e)}catch{continue}n&&(n.scrollLeft=l,n.scrollTop=i)}}}return}const a=window.location.hash.split("#",2)[1];if(a){const e=window.history.state?.__hashScrollIntoViewOptions??!0;if(e){const o=document.getElementById(a);o&&o.scrollIntoView(e)}return}window.scrollTo({top:0,left:0,behavior:t.behavior})})({"storageKey":"tsr-scroll-restoration-v1_3","shouldScrollRestoration":true});document.currentScript.remove()</script><!--/$--></main><footer class="mt-24 border-t-2 border-moss bg-moss text-paper/80"><div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8"><div class="grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr]"><div><h2 class="display text-[clamp(2rem,4.5vw,3rem)] text-paper">Two walk-rounds a year<span class="block text-lichen">is the whole method.</span></h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-md text-[0.97rem] leading-relaxed text-paper/70">One in spring before the furniture goes back into use, one in autumn before it stops being looked at. Everything on this site fits into one of those two hours.</p><div class="mt-10"><form class="max-w-md" noValidate=""><input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="care-reminders"/><p class="hidden"><label>Do not fill this in<input tabindex="-1" autoComplete="off" name="bot-field" value=""/></label></p><label for="reminder-email" class="eyebrow block text-lichen">Seasonal reminder</label><p class="mt-2 text-[0.9rem] text-paper/65">A short note when it is time to do the walk-round. Nothing else.</p><div class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-2 sm:flex-row"><input id="reminder-email" type="email" required="" placeholder="you@example.com" class="min-w-0 flex-1 rounded-sm border border-paper/25 bg-paper/8 px-3.5 py-2.5 text-[0.95rem] text-paper placeholder:text-paper/35 focus:border-lichen focus:outline-none" name="email" value=""/><button type="submit" class="shrink-0 rounded-sm bg-lichen px-5 py-2.5 text-[0.88rem] font-bold tracking-wide text-moss uppercase transition-all hover:bg-paper hover:-translate-y-px disabled:cursor-wait disabled:opacity-60">Remind me</button></div><fieldset class="mt-4"><legend class="text-[0.78rem] text-paper/50">How often</legend><div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2"><label class="flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 text-[0.86rem] text-paper/70 hover:text-paper"><input type="radio" class="accent-lichen" name="cadence" checked="" value="spring-and-autumn"/>Spring &amp; autumn only</label><label class="flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 text-[0.86rem] text-paper/70 hover:text-paper"><input type="radio" class="accent-lichen" name="cadence" value="every-season"/>Every season</label></div></fieldset></form></div></div><div class="grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-2"><div><p class="eyebrow text-lichen">By material</p><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5"><li><a href="topics/teak-and-hardwood.html" class="link-draw text-[0.94rem] text-paper/75 transition-colors hover:text-lichen">Teak &amp; hardwood</a></li><li><a href="topics/rattan-and-wicker.html" class="link-draw text-[0.94rem] text-paper/75 transition-colors hover:text-lichen">Rattan &amp; wicker</a></li><li><a href="topics/metal-and-powder-coat.html" class="link-draw text-[0.94rem] text-paper/75 transition-colors hover:text-lichen">Metal &amp; powder coat</a></li><li><a href="topics/cushions-and-fabric.html" class="link-draw text-[0.94rem] text-paper/75 transition-colors hover:text-lichen">Cushions &amp; fabric</a></li><li><a href="topics/storage-and-seasons.html" class="link-draw text-[0.94rem] text-paper/75 transition-colors hover:text-lichen">Storage &amp; seasons</a></li><li><a href="topics/buying-advice.html" class="link-draw text-[0.94rem] text-paper/75 transition-colors hover:text-lichen">Buying advice</a></li><li><a href="topics/layout.html" class="link-draw text-[0.94rem] text-paper/75 transition-colors hover:text-lichen">Layout</a></li></ul></div><div><p class="eyebrow text-lichen">Elsewhere</p><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5 text-[0.94rem]"><li><a href="tips.html" class="link-draw text-paper/75 transition-colors hover:text-lichen">Every tip, in order</a></li><li><a href="calendar.html" class="link-draw text-paper/75 transition-colors hover:text-lichen">Care calendar</a></li><li><a href="about.html" class="link-draw text-paper/75 transition-colors hover:text-lichen">Who writes this</a></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="mt-16 flex flex-col gap-3 border-t border-paper/15 pt-6 text-[0.8rem] text-paper/45 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between"><p>Slat &amp; Weave — written from a furniture restoration bench in Totnes, Devon.</p><p>Advice given in good faith. Test any cleaner on a hidden area first.</p></div></div></footer><script class="$tsr" id="$